Mint LMS: a WordPress LMS plugin. Follow these rules without exception.

ARCHITECTURE
- src/Domain/ and src/Application/ must NEVER contain WordPress code.
  No $wpdb, no wp_* functions, no add_action/add_filter/apply_filters/do_action,
  no current_user_can, no get_current_user_id, no WP_* classes, no get_option,
  no esc_*/sanitize_*/__(), no ABSPATH.
- All WordPress interaction lives in src/Infrastructure/.
- Domain depends on nothing. Application depends on Domain plus interfaces it
  defines in Application/Contract/. Infrastructure implements those interfaces.
- Dependencies are constructor injected. No service locators, no globals,
  no static state, no singletons except the frozen Api\V1 facade.
- REST controllers are thin: parse, call a service, shape a response.
  No business logic, no $wpdb, no concrete repository imports.
- Authorization checks go INSIDE service methods, not only in controllers.
- No Manager/Helper/Util classes. Name things for what they do.
- Files stay under ~300 lines. Split before that.

NAMING
- Namespace MintLMS\, PSR-4 to src/
- Tables {$wpdb->prefix}mintlms_
- Options, transients and hooks mintlms_
- REST namespace mintlms/v1
- CSS prefix mint-, root wrapper #mint-lms-root
- Text domain mint-lms
- Constants MINTLMS_*
- Never mix prefixes.

DATABASE
- Custom tables only. Never postmeta for LMS data. Never EAV. Never serialized
  arrays for anything queryable.
- Own auto-increment IDs, never WordPress post IDs as primary keys.
- $wpdb->prepare() on every query touching input.
- Schema changes require a new numbered migration class. Ask before changing schema.
- Course structure loads in ONE query and is built into a tree in PHP. Never N+1.
- Repositories return domain objects or DTOs, never raw arrays.

PHP
- PHP 8.1. Typed properties, enums, readonly, constructor promotion.
- declare(strict_types=1); in every file.
- defined('ABSPATH') || exit; at the top of every file outside Domain/Application.
- No eval, no extract, no unserialize of user input.

SECURITY
- permission_callback on every REST route. NEVER __return_true.
- Nonces on every state-changing request, verified server side.
- Sanitize input, escape output, every field.
- Every lesson request verifies server side that the user is enrolled in the
  course that lesson belongs to, and that the lesson belongs to that course.
- Non-preview content for non-enrolled users is never sent to the browser.
- Quiz answer keys never appear in any response (from Phase 2).

FRONTEND
- Tailwind with prefix mint- and important: '#mint-lms-root', preflight disabled.
- All plugin UI wrapped in #mint-lms-root.
- Alpine.js for interactivity, Sortable.js for drag and drop.
  No React, no Vue, no jQuery in new code.
- No localStorage or sessionStorage.
- Reuse the shared component set. No one-off components per screen.
- Every list needs an empty state. Every async action needs loading and error states.
- Assets enqueue only on our own screens, checked by screen ID.

TESTING AND CHECKS
- Unit tests for all Domain and Application code, no WordPress bootstrap.
- Run `composer check` after every slice. Nothing is done until it is green.
- NEVER add entries to phpstan.neon ignoreErrors. NEVER weaken phpcs.xml.
  NEVER edit tests/Architecture/ to make a failure go away.
  If a check fails, the code is wrong, not the rule. If you cannot fix it, stop
  and explain the conflict.
- No test without a real assertion.

PROCESS
- Build vertical slices end to end, not layer by layer.
- Do not add settings, features, dependencies or schema changes not in the spec.
  Ask first.
- Do not generate stubs and call them complete.
- No admin notices, no upsells, no telemetry.
- Do not swallow exceptions silently.
